wildos-cooler (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The GPU's temperature is read on PCs with NVIDIA's own driver packages,
    which leave out nvidia-smi: Cooler now asks the driver's NVML library.
  * With the GPU chosen, the name above the number says GPU.
  * With both chosen, the CPU's and the GPU's temperatures stand side by
    side, each with its name, instead of taking turns. Last minute still
    takes turns, as its line follows one temperature.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000

wildos-cooler (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Choose whose temperature the cooler's screen shows: the CPU, the GPU,
    or both taking turns every five seconds (Screen, Temperature).
  * The smaller writing on every face is larger, so it can be read on the
    cooler's screen.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000

wildos-cooler (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * When Wild OS shuts down or restarts, Cooler finishes the picture it is
    sending to the cooler's screen before it lets go, so the cooler is not
    left half way through one.
  * The RGB ring face shows on PCs with an NVIDIA graphics card.

 -- Wild OS Developers <dev@wildos.io>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0000

